NAMESPACES
============

IF we create any pod any it will get created on default namespaces

kubectl get namespace --------------> command to get list of name spaces

kubectl get ns --------------> command to get list of name spaces



kubectl describe pod podname --------------> command to view in which namespaces it will be present

kubectl get po -n kube-system --------------> command to view in namespaces which present in the name of kube-system

kubectl get deploy -n kube-system --------------> command to view deployments which present in the name of kube-system

kubectl get svc -n kube-system --------------> command to view services which present in the name of kube-system

kubectl get all -n kube-system --------------> command to view all resources present in the name of kube-system


lets discuss about kube-public
===============================

will be able to see the pod which present in one particular namespace and also the same with another namespace -------> NO

it should be available for everyone on every namespace -----------> here we will use kube-public

