COFIG MAPS
===============

to create config maps 

we have 4 types under below

1. literal (values -------> command)
2. file (data)
3. env file (values) ------->cm create
4. declarative --------> means manifest file

lets do how to create 


kubectl cm cm1 --from-literal=name=mustafa --from-literal=company=babu --from-place-literal=place=hyderabad ---------------> command to create config map

cm --------> config map, cm1 -------> comfig map name

kubectl get cm -----------> command to view list of congig map

kubectl describe cm babu(configmap name) -----------> command to view full info & data of config map

2. through file

vim mydata

welcome to cm file
we are adding some values here
this is going to inside of the pod

:wq

kubectl create cm cm2 --from-file=mydata -----------> command to execute above file


kubectl get cm -----------> command to view list of cm

kubectl describe cm cm2 ------------> command to see the data in cm


